      "math_academy_id": "e-12731",
      "problem": "Write down $\\lnot P(x)$ given that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130746/assets/ed810318e9b5d6e76b77735530ff9312af66f936d7c8e197d6dd0fb99227dcb8.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "The symbol \"$\\neg$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130746/assets/976e6fe9a107732c81210776e49cfe3f68939512c0fad63739e2f59acb17f109.svg) \n\nIn other words, $x$ is smaller than $10.$ Therefore, $\\neg P(x)$ means the following:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130746/assets/dca132f34f73e2f5987a803e592c1f664cc790ed83ec204205975c401280038c.svg)",
